    {
      "id": "Ugzr0o7jwtNGWawijIJ4AaABAg",
      "author": "@TheEarthEngineOfficial",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/A-8pdPY1MNP00I1rBiYVsY53_o6F6OjbYyWuaDf2OGeL0Dz-YDTufnOuZ12M2n5zSzyVod-a=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "The Congo–Nile divide detail really stood out — two neighbours sharing the same plateau and the same colonial starting point, yet one ends up with the lake and the old capital while the other bets everything on gorilla permits and clean governance. It makes me wonder how much of the gap is geography and how much is the choices made after 1994. The $300-per-person crossover point was the most striking number in the whole video.",
